    "text": "The 34% context contamination variance was estimated from a meta-analysis of studies where per-session context isolation was not uniformly applied.",
    "topic": "Measurement conditions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Proper session controls are defined as at least: clearing conversation memory between trials, randomizing condition order, and preventing cross-contamination through shared model state.",
    "topic": "Operational definition of session controls"
  },
  {
    "text": "In studies that enforced strict session isolation, context contamination variance dropped to under 5% of total variance.",
    "topic": "Impact of controls"
  },
  {
    "text": "The claim of invalidity in statements A and B applies to comparative conclusions drawn from uncontrolled studies but does not extend to those with documented session hygiene protocols.",
    "topic": "Scope of validity claim"
  }
]
